READ ME

Ancestral State Reconstruction.R is the code file used for the analyses in R.

GroupNames.csv states all species names in the analysis. The end of the file represents which part of the project it is used in:

None of the below - Fanning Method on Original Sample Size of 162
1 - Fanning Method on Increase Sample Size of 244
S - Swimming Method on Original Sample Size of 162
1S - Swimming Method on Increase Sample Size of 244

For the rest of the files if there is not a 1 it is for Fanning and Swimming on the original sample size of 162. If there is a 1 it is on the larger sample size of 244.

ConsensusTree.nex - The consensus tree.

AncestralStatesContinuous.csv - Column 1: Species Names. Column 2: PC1 Values. Column 3: PC2 Values.

AncestralStatesDiscrete.csv - Column 1: Species Names. Column 2: Fanning State (1 = Non-Fanning, 2 = Fanning). Column 3: Swimming State (1 = Non-Pectoral Swimming, 2 = Pectoral Swimming, 3 = No data).

HarmonicArray.csv and HarmonicArray1 were used for the Kmult statistics and were generated from the morphospace in MATLAB.
